# Files consumed by Linux must check out with LF whatever the committing
# machine's core.autocrlf says.
#
# The blobs are correct today because this repo is committed from a box with
# core.autocrlf=true. That is a property of one machine's git config, not of
# the repository, and the failure it guards against is both cryptic and total:
# a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named
# `bash\r`, so scripts/run_cycle.sh dies with
#
#     /srv/bvp/scripts/run_cycle.sh: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter
#
# and systemd mis-parses unit values with a trailing CR without saying so.
# Both would present on the server as "the deployment is broken" with nothing
# pointing at line endings.

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf
*.template  text eol=lf
